<title>USA: Clinton names diplomat ambassador to Mozambique.</title>
<headline>Clinton names diplomat ambassador to Mozambique.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton plans to nominate career foreign service officer Brian Dean Curran as U.S. ambassador to Mozambique, the White House said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Curran joined the U.S. foreign service in 1973 and has served in Niger, Guinea Bissau, Belgium, France and Ireland.</p>
